        null
    ],
    "optionsVersion": 1,
    "apiVersion": "VERSION_0",
    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Tests whether variants differ from the control on conversion rate (z-test) or mean (Welch's t-test), with lift, confidence intervals, p-values, verdicts and required sample size.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Statistics",
    "tags": [
        "a/b test",
        "experiment",
        "significance",
        "t-test",
        "z-test",
        "conversion",
        "lift",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Tells you whether a variant really beat the control, or whether the difference could be chance.\n\n- **Conversion rates** (did the visitor buy, click, sign up?): two-proportion z-test\n- **Means** (order value, time on page, basket size): Welch's t-test, which does not assume equal variances\n- Each variant is compared with the **control**: difference, **relative lift**, **confidence interval**, **p-value**, *Significant* yes / no and a **plain-language verdict**\n- **Sample size needed** per variant to confirm an effect of the observed size at the chosen power\n- Optional **segments** (device, country, channel) with a **Bonferroni correction** for running many comparisons\n- Data either **one row per visitor** (variant and outcome; outcomes such as Yes / No, 1 / 0, true / false are understood) or **one row per variant** (visitors and conversions)\n\nThe second output gives each variant's sample size, rate or mean and its confidence interval.\n\nCompares two groups on rates or means in one step. Pure Python: no packages to install.",
    "dependencies": "",
